▲  Storybook found TypeScript 7.0.2 as the `typescript` package.
│  TypeScript 7 does not include the compiler API that Storybook uses to
│  read your component types for Controls and the Docs args table.

│  If package.json has no `typescript` entry, your package manager
│  installed TypeScript 7 for Storybook's peer dependency. Add
│  `typescript@^6` to the devDependencies in package.json.

│  If your project uses TypeScript 7, install TypeScript 7 and TypeScript
│  6 side by side. In package.json, replace the `typescript` entry in
│  devDependencies with these two entries:

│  "@typescript/native": "npm:typescript@^7.0.2",
│  "typescript": "npm:@typescript/typescript6@^6.0.2"

│  `tsc` stays on TypeScript 7, and the `typescript` package is
│  TypeScript 6. Both entries are necessary.

│  Then install dependencies and restart Storybook.

│  Until then, Storybook falls back to the deprecated builder docgen with
│  `react-docgen`, which will be removed in Storybook 12.

│  More info:
│  https://storybook.js.org/docs/configure/integration/typescript?ref=error#typescript-7

